Short:        UTF-8 Unicode text editor with Emoji + gadgets
Author:       krabobmkd
Uploader:     victorien.ferry@free.fr
Type:         text/edit
Version:      3.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2
Requires:     68020, AmigaOS 3.2.x, 8 MB Fast RAM

Version 3 corrects three causes of memory corruption present in version 2.x:
the rendering library, the text editor gadget, and the button gadget now all
use proper Exec Signal Semaphores for inter-process safety instead of
Forbid()/Permit() pairs.  Applications, gadgets and the library are all
significantly more stable as a result.

EmojiGear is a UTF-8 Unicode text editor for AmigaOS 3.2.x (68020+).
It renders TrueType/OpenType fonts and displays full-colour Emoji,
on any Amiga Video mode, native or RTG, indexed or true color.
Fonts settings allow to manage a list of cascading fonts so you
can have both a font for text and one for Emojis, 
 and display and convert any modern text correctly.

  - Antialias, preference for background and pen colours, 
  - Multiple documents open in a tab bar.  
  - Load and save UTF-8, ISO Latin-1, ISO Latin-2; auto-detect UTF-16.
  - Find & Replace, Undo/Redo, 
  - optional word wrap
  - optional ANSI escape rendering for unix shell compatible display
  - configurable font size with ctrl+- keys. 
  - Emoji Box allowing to choose 8 sets of 40 emojis mapped to F keys. 
  - You can "pipe" the output of another command into the editor.
  - Settings saved in icon tooltypes
  - Many corrections and improvements since the first release
  
Beyond the editor, the package installs three reusable Amiga components
that any developer can open from their own application:
  utf8rastport.library  -- FreeType 2 Unicode rendering on any RastPort,
                          with font fallback chains and colour Emoji.
  unitexteditor.gadget  -- the full editor as a BOOPSI gadget class,
                          embeddable in any application window.
  unibutton.gadget      -- a push-button gadget with Unicode/Emoji labels.

  SDK, developer docs and examples are optionaly installed,
  there are example for a MUI integration, lib and gadget use.


 License is GPL for the lib and LGPL for the gadgets.


About OS 3.9 compatibility:

utf8rastport.library and unibutton.gadget are expected to work correctly
on AmigaOS 3.9 and even AmigaOS 3.1, and can be used as standalone SDK
components by applications targeting those older systems.

Full compatibility for unitexteditor.gadget cannot be achieved on OS 3.9.
The gadget uses offscreen bitmap tile rendering via a shared Layer, and
there is a known bug in layers.library on OS 3.9 that makes this pattern
unsafe.  This bug was fixed in AmigaOS 3.2.  Using unitexteditor.gadget
or the EmojiGear application on OS 3.9 may cause display corruption or
system instability.

OS 3.9 users may try the MUImojiGear variant included in this package.
MUI manages its own rendering and avoids the layers issue, but intensive
Unicode rendering may eventually make the system unstable on OS 3.9.

The best solution is to upgrade: the official AmigaOS 3.2 installer from
Hyperion Entertainment can be applied to any OS 3.9 system and corrects
a large number of OS 3.9 bugs including the layers.library issue.


 
